# FUNDA360 TESTING STRATEGY & QUALITY ASSURANCE MASTER PLAN (TSQAMP)

## 1. Executive Summary
This Testing Strategy & Quality Assurance Master Plan defines the processes, standards, and responsibilities required to ensure Funda360 meets enterprise SaaS quality expectations. It integrates testing into every phase of the software development lifecycle, establishes quality gates, and provides a framework for continuous improvement. The plan ensures reliability, scalability, accessibility, and compliance with POPIA and international standards.

---

## 2. Quality Objectives
- **Reliability:** 99.9% uptime, minimal downtime.
- **Low Defect Rates:** < 0.5 defects per 1,000 lines of code.
- **Usability:** Task completion rate > 90%.
- **Accessibility:** WCAG 2.2 AA compliance.
- **Security Assurance:** Zero critical vulnerabilities at release.
- **Performance:** Response times < 3 seconds for 95% of requests.
- **Scalability:** Support millions of learners across thousands of schools.
- **Maintainability:** Modular, testable codebase.
- **Compliance:** POPIA and audit requirements.
- **Customer Satisfaction:** CSAT > 85%.

---

## 3. Quality Principles
- **Shift Left Testing:** Testing begins at requirements and design phases.
- **Test Pyramid:** Unit > Integration > E2E > UI tests.
- **Risk-Based Testing:** Prioritize high-risk modules (finance, HR, authentication).
- **Continuous Testing:** Automated tests integrated into CI/CD.
- **Automation First:** Maximize automation for regression and performance.
- **Manual Exploratory Testing:** Human-driven discovery of edge cases.
- **Regression Prevention:** Automated regression suites.
- **Traceability:** Link requirements → tests → defects → releases.
- **Quality Ownership:** Shared responsibility across teams.
- **Defect Prevention:** Root cause analysis and proactive measures.

